# digest.vec — conformance vectors for the `digest` family.
#
# ONE FILE, EVERY IMPLEMENTATION. The engine's src/Digest.cpp, Digest::Native's
# C, and that distribution's ecosystem fallback are separate implementations on
# purpose — see NATIVE-MODULES-PLAN, "The architecture: independent C". This
# file is the thing that keeps them honest, so it is read by all of them and
# weakened by none of them.
#
# THIS COPY IS THE MASTER. It moved here from Digest-Native/t/vectors/ when
# DATA-PLAN P3 landed and the engine became the primary implementation
# (NATIVE-MODULES-PLAN's order of work, step 1). The distribution keeps a copy
# so a published tarball stands alone; t/regression/data-native-digest.raku
# checks the two are byte-identical whenever both are present, so a vector
# added on one side cannot quietly fail to reach the other.
#
# Generated by tools/gen-vectors.raku from the system openssl, never from our
# own code. Every published constant it contains was also checked by eye
# against RFC 1321, FIPS 180-4, RFC 2202 and RFC 4231.
#
#   H <algo> <input> <expected-hex>
#   M <algo> <blocksize|-> <key> <message> <expected-hex>
#
# <input>, <key> and <message> are hex, optionally <hex>*<count> for a repeat,
# and `-` for empty. A blocksize of `-` means the algorithm's own (RFC 2104),
# which is what this family uses when the caller does not say.

